    {
      "id": "claim_fbfa5df623a744d086aa2b266414de51",
      "statement": "Each workspace's Overseer DO holds a real git object database (SHA-1, zlib-deflated loose objects byte-identical to git's own) in the gitObjects typed-storage collection, driven through isomorphic-git's plumbing only; there is deliberately no ref layer — gadget records' commitIds, blueprint records, and chats' pinned commits are the refs — and one store per workspace mixes all gadgets' histories, deduplicating related histories at the blob/tree level.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/git-store.ts#L1-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:561e34821b644f47788ccff3959b10693497ef2d4edffa6086bdb38a15581927:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://plans/git-storage.md#L14-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:868ebf5f3f685a81b0bf7c355707450d7b0ae6e2311d5b2d0c1cc1839fc020cc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_45f6a421bd2f430e84bced897f33b749",
      "statement": "isomorphic-git's porcelain is off-limits (git.commit hard-requires HEAD/index/config and git.merge cannot represent the needed merge behavior); the fs shim maps loose-object paths onto the collection and rejects everything else, must implement all ten fs methods (bindFs binds unconditionally), must answer the promise-detection probe with a rejected promise, and must reject missing files with code ENOENT; object writes are idempotent and the DO's single-threaded execution plus output gate provide serialization.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/git-store.ts#L76-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dfc260b6de5a8dcb0cb81528c59ddf04fe072d5ea9e1677c520f34080ef572d8:"
        },
        {
