    },
    {
      "id": "claim_04832bd3f88b4371bb5977b639e0af5f",
      "statement": "The OT priority convention is fixed here and used identically on both sides of the wire: for two concurrent changes against the same revision, the change the server ordered earlier comes first (its inserts precede the later change's at equal positions), which is exactly ChangeSet's transform law; transformCodeChange bakes the pairing in and nothing else may call the underlying map.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/code-change.ts#L18-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b6f0e8eb54be9c3811e8a20505806058072fe0450f714bc4130d9a1c4fcbe03d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4f038f20927b46bcb00f7033823d2cf4",
      "statement": "Change validation is two-stage in a required order: validateCodeChangeSchema runs BEFORE any transform (transformation is structural and must only see well-formed changes), validateCodeChangeContent runs AFTER transforming to the server's current revision (lengths and boundaries are only meaningful against the content the change will apply to); the declared shape is established upstream by capnweb-validate at the RPC edge, so the stages check only what the type system cannot express.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/code-change.ts#L25-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e2dfec5cf173466e966504cba78debed138b3849105161200b669431ce2536a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_01434526d55544d9aea926369f61a10c",
      "statement": "ChatCodeBase describes the chat's stream identity: pins name the base commit each modified gadget edits against (unpinned gadgets track mainline head live), generation bumps are content-preserving (in-flight submissions transformed across) or destructive (clients discard and rebuild), epoch points at the epochBoundary/conversion message whose successors alone contribute, and submitCodeChange transforms over anything accepted since the submitter's revision while deduping by (clientId, seq) so retries must be byte-identical.",
      "evidence": [
