    {
      "id": "claim_c50a8913c5174ae285d8bff7c2afbcee",
      "statement": "Yjs is used only where bases are guaranteed byte-identical: seeding a chat's Y.Doc from a commit is deterministic because Yjs's only randomness is the clientID, which the seed fixes (with sorted file iteration in a single transaction) making encodeStateAsUpdateV2 a pure function of the file map, and Yjs's own collision handling makes a reserved clientID safe.",
