    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d024f90fc6e14b39bebdce5fcaa760c5",
      "statement": "The git migration (run in the Overseer constructor from the version singleton) replayed the legacy Yjs log once into per-gadget commit chains — commit points at every historical merge, every >=1-hour log gap, the final version, and every persisted pinned version, each chain rooted at a version-0 empty-tree commit so every permanent gadget left with a head — and converted each live chat in place into a conversionBoundary changes message (diff of the flattened legacy doc vs the anchor trees, with a pin per touched gadget); the boundary is written even when empty because ChatCodeBase.epoch points at it.",
      "evidence": [
